HST Office: a large ribbon menu button shows "Label ▾" under its image, as the large tool buttons do.

Owner report (15/11/2026, Writer ▸ Trang đầu ▸ Chỉnh sửa): "Chọn" drew VCL's menu arrow beside its icon and, being
centred as one block with a 16 px icon, its label sat higher than the labels of the large tool buttons beside it.
A large menu button (image above its label: Writer's Select, Sheets' Insert, Delete, Margins..., the menus of the
gap list G10) now lays its label out like the large buttons of the approved mockup: at most two lines under the
image, split at the space that balances them, ▾ at the end of the second line (alone on it after a short label),
and no arrow beside the image; the label stays its accessible name. At the small state it keeps the icon and
VCL's arrow, as before. Writer's Select and Sheets' Insert and Delete cells take their large icons.

